                <pb facs="1439" n="1415" xml:id="pg1415"/>
                <p rendition="#flush">I. <hi rendition="#italic">Records of Previous
                    Meetings</hi></p>
                <p>It was <hi rendition="#italic">decided</hi> to approve the records of the
                    decisions taken by the Council of Foreign Ministers at the 1st, 2nd, 3rd, 4th,
                    5th, 6th, 7th, 8th and 9th Meetings of the Third Session, held in New York.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">II. <hi rendition="#italic">Report of the Deputies</hi></p>
                <p>The report submitted by the Acting Chairman of the Deputies was considered. (See
                    CFM(D) (46) (NY) 127Meeting, December 4, 1946.)<anchor n="61" xml:id="d382-f1"
                    /></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">III. <hi rendition="#italic">Article 76 of the Draft Treaty
                        With Italy</hi></p>
                <p>It was <hi rendition="#italic">decided</hi> to adopt the text of Article 76
                    (Annex l).<anchor n="62" xml:id="d382-f2"/></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">IV. <hi rendition="#italic">Draft Peace Treaty With Italy,
                        Article 16 bis. Draft Instrument for the Provisional Regime</hi> (CFM(46)
                        (NY)43)<anchor n="63" xml:id="d382-f3"/></p>
                <p>1. <hi rendition="#italic">Article 14</hi> (now Article 10 in CFM(46) (NY)43
                    revised December 4)</p>
                <p>It was <hi rendition="#italic">decided</hi> to adopt the text of Paragraph 10 of
                    the Draft Instrument for the Provisional Regime annex to Article 16 bis (Annex
                    2).</p>
                <p>2. <hi rendition="#italic">Article 13</hi> (now Article 9 in CFM(46) (NY)43
                    revised December 4)</p>
                <p>After an exchange of views, it was <hi rendition="#italic">decided</hi> to refer
                    Paragraph 13 for joint study by the Sub-Committee on Trieste and the Economic
                    Experts.</p>
                <p>3. <hi rendition="#italic">Article 6</hi> (no change in number)</p>
                <p>It was <hi rendition="#italic">decided</hi> to approve the text submitted by the
                    Military Experts. (See CFM(46) (NY)48)<anchor n="64" xml:id="d382-f4"/></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">V. <hi rendition="#italic">Reparation by Italy for Yugoslavia,
                        Greece, Albania and Ethiopia and Reparation by Bulgaria for Yugoslavia and
                        Greece</hi></p>
                <p>After an exchange of views, a decision on this question was <hi
                        rendition="#italic">deferred.</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">VI. <hi rendition="#italic">Compensation for Damage to United
                        Nations’ Property on the Territory of Italy, Roumania, Hungary, Bulgaria and
                        Finland</hi></p>
                <p>After an exchange of views, a decision on this question was <hi
                        rendition="#italic">deferred.</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">VII. <hi rendition="#italic">Fair Prices-Reparation Deliveries
                        From Roumania</hi></p>
                <p>After an exchange of views a decision on this question was <hi
                        rendition="#italic">deferred.</hi></p>
